diff --git a/docs/HOST_SDL2_SURFACE.md b/docs/HOST_SDL2_SURFACE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8a22183
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/HOST_SDL2_SURFACE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Full launcher UI in an existing SDL2 window
+
+`RECOMP_LAUNCHER_HAS_HOST_SDL2_RENDERER_SURFACE` advertises an optional borrowed
+SDL2 surface. Set both appended `RecompLauncherCGameInfo` fields:
+
+```c
+gi.host_sdl_window = game_window;       /* SDL_Window* */
+gi.host_sdl_renderer = game_renderer;   /* SDL_Renderer* for that window */
+gi.in_session = 1;                     /* Resume and Quit Game semantics */
+int result = recomp_launcher_run_window(title, &settings, &gi, assets,
+                                        current_rom, rom_out, sizeof rom_out);
+```
+
+Pause gameplay and audio before this synchronous call. It pumps SDL events and
+renders the same dashboard, settings, controller, and other enabled panels using
+Dear ImGui's SDLRenderer2 backend. It does not create a window or OpenGL context,
+launch a process, or destroy the supplied SDL objects. On return, resume gameplay
+and apply the edited settings; handle the ordinary launcher result codes.
+
+The platform saves and restores render target, logical size, integer scaling,
+scale, viewport, clip rectangle, draw color, and draw blend mode. The previous
+Dear ImGui context is restored too. Fonts and artwork use SDL textures while
+attached; standalone invocations continue using OpenGL. Window sizing preferences
+are not saved from the borrowed surface. `SDL_Quit` is never called for it.
+
+Pass both pointers or neither. Invalid pairs return `RESULT_UNAVAILABLE`; they
+never fall back to creating a second window. This capability accepts SDL2
+objects only. SDL3 builds reject supplied borrowed SDL2 pointers.
+
+Hosts supplying their own Dear ImGui should provide a compatible SDLRenderer2
+backend or leave recomp-ui to compile its bundled backend. If the host already
+links that backend, set CMake variable `RECOMP_UI_HOST_SDLRENDERER2=ON` to avoid
+duplicate symbols. SDL2 2.0.17 or newer is required by the renderer backend.
+
+`recomp-ui-host-surface-test` covers attachment, artwork upload, renderer state
+and ownership. `recomp-ui-host-surface-ui-test` renders and captures the full
+dashboard, settings and controller views with a software renderer and asserts
+that no second SDL window was created.
